  "question": {
    "text": "Let $(2,3)$ be the largest open interval in which the function $f(x)=2 \\log _{\\mathrm{e}}(x-2)-x^2+a x+1$ is strictly increasing and (b, c) be the largest open interval, in which the function $\\mathrm{g}(x)=(x-1)^3(x+2-\\mathrm{a})^2$ is strictly decreasing. Then $100(a+b-c)$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OSg3f",
      "text": "420",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LSuEK",
      "text": "360",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
